Method: fr.baretto.ollamassist.chat.rag.DocumentIndexingPipeline#handleDocumentError
Signature: private void handleDocumentError(String filePath, Exception e)
Body: {
    int retryCount = fileRetries.computeIfAbsent(filePath, k -> new AtomicInteger(0)).incrementAndGet();
    if (retryCount <= MAX_RETRIES) {
        log.warn(String.format(REQUEUE_LOG_FORMAT, retryCount, MAX_RETRIES, filePath));
        reQueueDocument(filePath);
    } else {
        log.error(String.format(PERMANENT_FAILURE_FORMAT, MAX_RETRIES, filePath));
        pendingDocumentIds.remove(filePath);
        fileRetries.remove(filePath);
    }
    if (e instanceof CorruptedIndexException) {
        handleCorruption();
    }
}


Type: class fr.baretto.ollamassist.agent.tools.files.FilePathGuard
Doc: * Resolves and confines file paths to the project root directory.
 *
 * <p>Prevents path traversal attacks: any path that resolves outside
 * {@code project.getBasePath()} (e.g. {@code /etc/passwd}, {@code ../../.ssh/id_rsa})
 * is rejected with a {@link PathTraversalException}.
 *
 * <p>All file tools must call {@link #resolveConfined} instead of
 * implementing their own {@code resolveAbsolute} logic.
Method: public static Path resolveConfined(String path, Project project)
Method: public static Path resolveConfined(String path, String basePath)
Method: private static void checkAncestorConfinement(Path path, Path root, String originalPath, String basePath)


Method: fr.baretto.ollamassist.agent.tools.files.FilePathGuard#checkAncestorConfinement
Doc: * Walks up {@code path}'s ancestor chain until it finds a directory that exists on disk,
     * then verifies that its real path (after resolving all symlinks) is still within {@code root}.
     * This guards against a symlinked parent directory escaping the project boundary.
Signature: private static void checkAncestorConfinement(Path path, Path root, String originalPath, String basePath)
Body: {
    Path realRoot;
    try {
        realRoot = root.toRealPath();
    } catch (IOException e) {
        realRoot = root;
    }
    Path ancestor = path.getParent();
    while (ancestor != null) {
        try {
            Path realAncestor = ancestor.toRealPath();
            if (!realAncestor.startsWith(realRoot)) {
                throw new PathTraversalException(originalPath, basePath);
            }
            // Found an existing, confined ancestor — we're good.
            return;
        } catch (PathTraversalException ex) {
            // Re-throw security exception immediately.
            throw ex;
        } catch (IOException ex) {
            // This ancestor doesn't exist either; go up one more level.
            ancestor = ancestor.getParent();
        }
    }
}


Type: class fr.baretto.ollamassist.agent.tools.files.PathTraversalException extends SecurityException
Doc: * Thrown when a path resolves to a location outside the project root.


Method: fr.baretto.ollamassist.agent.tools.files.FilePathGuard#resolveConfined
Doc: * Resolves {@code path} relative to {@code basePath} and verifies confinement.
     * Exposed as package-visible for unit testing without an IntelliJ Platform runtime.
     *
     * @param path     a relative or absolute path string
     * @param basePath the project root as a string
     * @return the normalized, confined absolute path
Signature: public static Path resolveConfined(String path, String basePath)
Body: {
    if (path == null) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("path must not be null");
    }
    if (basePath == null || basePath.isBlank()) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("Project base path is not available");
    }
    Path root = Paths.get(basePath).normalize().toAbsolutePath();
    Path resolved = Paths.get(path).isAbsolute() ? Paths.get(path).normalize() : root.resolve(path).normalize();
    if (!resolved.startsWith(root)) {
        throw new PathTraversalException(path, basePath);
    }
    // Follow the full symlink chain to prevent escape via intermediate symlinks
    // (e.g. A → B → /etc/passwd).
    try {
        Path realResolved = resolved.toRealPath();
        Path realRoot;
        try {
            realRoot = root.toRealPath();
        } catch (IOException e2) {
            realRoot = root;
        }
        if (!realResolved.startsWith(realRoot)) {
            throw new PathTraversalException(path, basePath);
        }
    } catch (IOException e) {
        // The target file does not exist yet (valid for write operations).
        // Walk up ancestor directories until we find one that exists, then verify
        // its real path is still within the project root.  This prevents a symlink
        // in an ancestor directory from escaping confinement when the target file
        // is created for the first time (SI-1 / A3).
        checkAncestorConfinement(resolved, root, path, basePath);
    }
    return resolved;
}

